  "markscheme": {
    "html": "<section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"a.i\"><p><strong>a.i</strong></p><p>Use of F = BIL OR F/L = BI ✓ = 1.0 «N m<sup>−1</sup>» ✓</p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"a.ii\"><p><strong>a.ii</strong></p><p>Arrow drawn perpendicular (by eye) as shown.  ✓   Arrow can be drawn anywhere along the wire.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_05\"><img alt=\"Source markscheme diagram 5\" src=\"asset:fig_05\"/></figure></p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"b.i\"><p><strong>b.i</strong></p><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{F}{L}=\\frac{\\mu _{0}}{2\\pi}\\frac{I_{R} I_{Z}}{r}\"></span> AND <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{F}{L}=B_{R} I_{Z}\"></span> ✓ Combine to give the result ✓   Must see subscripts on both I and B for full marks. Award [1 max] for correct derivations with incomplete subscripts.</p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"b.ii\"><p><strong>b.ii</strong></p><p>kg m s<sup>−2 </sup>A<sup>−2</sup> ✓   Allow fractional answers such as: <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{kg m}{s^{2} A^{2}}\"></span></p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"c.i\"><p><strong>c.i</strong></p><p>the magnetic field produced by the wire/I<sub>R</sub> is constant. ✓ therefore the «magnetic» flux/field through the coil is constant. ✓</p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"c.ii\"><p><strong>c.ii</strong></p><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\Delta  B = \\frac{{\\mu }_{0}}{2 \\pi } ( \\frac{10 - 2}{0.1} )\"></span> OR <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2\\times 10^{-5}-4\\times 10^{-6}=1.6\\times 10^{-5}\"></span>«<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"T\"></span>» ✓ <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\Delta  \\phi  = A \\Delta  B = ( \\pi  ) ( {0.02}^{2} ) ( ( 2 \\times  {10}^{- 5} ) - ( 4 \\times  {10}^{- 6} ) ) = 2.5 \\times  {10}^{- 8} - 5.03 \\times  {10}^{- 9}\"></span> = 2.01 × 10<sup>−8</sup> «Wb» ✓ <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\mathcal{E}  = \\frac{n \\Delta  \\phi }{\\Delta  t} = \\frac{( 20 ) ( 2.01 \\times  {10}^{- 8} )}{0.5} = 8.0 \\times  {10}^{- 7}\"></span>«<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"V\"></span>» ✓</p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"c.iii\"><p><strong>c.iii</strong></p><p>Anticlockwise/counter clockwise/CCW ✓ magnetic field from the wire is «increasing» into the page OR induced field must be out of the page ✓</p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"d\"><p><strong>d</strong></p><p>sine graph with half the period, i.e. one large square/5 small squares (by eye) ✓ and twice the amplitude, i.e. four small squares (by eye) ✓</p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"e.i\"><p><strong>e.i</strong></p><p>use of qvB = mv<sup>2</sup>/r OR <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"r=\\frac{mv}{qB}\"></span> ✓ <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1.6\\times 10^{-19}\\times 4.0\\times 10^{-6}=\\frac{9.11\\times 10^{-31}\\times 9\\times 10^{5}}{r}\"></span> OR <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"r=\\frac{9.11\\times 10^{-31}9\\times 10^{5}}{1.6\\times 10^{-19}4\\times 10^{-6}}\"></span> ✓ r = 1.28 OR 1.3 «m» ✓</p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"e.ii\"><p><strong>e.ii</strong></p><p>Force/Field decreases as electron moves away from the wire ✓ Hence radius increases. ✓</p></section>"
